            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a budget, then the Hindi for to collect (money owed)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पर्ची",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पर्ची — parcī — \"a slip (of paper), a chit\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बैंक में पहले एक पर्ची भरिए। baiṅk meṁ pahle ek parcī bhariye. At the bank, fill in a slip first."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पर्ची (parcī) is usually traced to Persian parča, \"a piece, a scrap\", with the Hindi ending -ī for a small one: a slip for a bank, a doctor or a lottery."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
